  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Session Rerun",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n`dsh-session-rerun` is an installable [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) Web plugin for inspecting and replaying a completed session Step."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Groups the durable session timeline by Turn and Step.\n- Shows model replies, tool calls, Skills, failures, and elapsed time.\n- Displays referenced script and Markdown filenames as compact badges on the right side of each Step.\n- Replays a top-level Step in a new session without changing the source session.\n- Replays a selected Subagent Step through a new main session in the original workspace. The new main Agent keeps only the recreated delegation, waits for the new child, and continues from that child's result."
    },
    {
      "section": "From npm (recommended)",
      "text": "```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile web add \\\n  dsh-client-ui-session-rerun \\\n  --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/\n```\n\nFor DSH Desktop, use the same package with the Desktop profile:\n\n```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile desktop add \\\n  dsh-client-ui-session-rerun \\\n  --registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "From GitHub",
      "text": "```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile web add \\\n  github:liuyangdongdong/dsh-session-rerun\n```\n\nReplace `--profile web` with `--profile desktop` to install the GitHub build in DSH Desktop."
    },
    {
      "section": "Start Web",
      "text": "```sh\nnpx @deepseek-ai/dsh web\n```\n\nRestart an already running Web process after installing or replacing the plugin."
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "The plugin never mutates the source session. A successful replay creates a new main session in the source workspace and opens it in the Web UI."
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "For a normal Step, the new Agent receives the durable history before the selected Step and that Step's logged user input. For a Subagent Step, the plugin creates a new main session and a new child session. The child replays the selected Step, while the new main session reconstructs only the delegation call, waits for the child, receives the new child result, and then continues."
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "Nested Subagent replay is intentionally unsupported. A Step must exist and have a matching `step/end` event before it can be replayed.\n\nSee [Architecture](docs/architecture.md) for the package split and lifecycle."
    },
    {
      "section": "Packages",
      "text": "| Package | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `dsh-client-ui-session-rerun` | Installable Web bundle, timeline projection, replay controls, and file badges |\n| `dsh-session-rerun` | Host Remote that reads durable sessions and creates replay sessions |\n\nThe root package declares `dsh.bundle.patch` in `package.json`; `cordis.patch.yml` mounts both roles. This follows the Harness profile and bundle model without modifying `agent-loop`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Requirements: Node.js `^22.19.0 || >=24.0.0` and pnpm `11.7.0`.\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm typecheck\npnpm test\npnpm pack:check\n\nThe committed `lib/` artifacts make npm and GitHub installations executable without an install-time build. The Web client artifact uses the DeepSeek Harness module-loader bundle format; regenerate it with a compatible Harness checkout after changing browser source."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
